rwtest 1
test "Projectile retargets" project="Bernael" group="Weapon" created=2026-09-17T00:00:00

# SoulLanternProjectileExtension: maxRetargets 1, retargetOnDowned true.
# A target that is already down counts as replaceable in TargetNeedsReplacement,
# and TryRetarget looks for the next hostile pawn in range that is still up. So
# the shot at A has to hit B.
#
# The proof is the burn on B, whom nobody shot at. A stays down and does not
# fight back, so the order stays stable.
#
# The assert is a proxy, not the thing itself: a retarget leaves no trace in
# game state, and nothing here can read intendedTarget off a bullet in flight.
# So this file cannot tell "retargeted and missed" from "never retargeted" -
# that claim belongs to a person and is asked in "Projectile arcs and bends".
#
# What stays here is the hit, and it must not fail for the hit roll instead:
# ResolveRetargetedShot aims on at 0.5 and throws a wild miss otherwise, so a
# single burst is a coin toss. Only the count of shots buys that away, as in
# "Lantern shot burns target": one cycle is 320 ticks (warmup 120, burst 5x20,
# RangedWeapon_Cooldown 120) plus about 18 ticks of flight, so 1320 ticks are
# four cycles and about twenty retargeted shots.
#
# Waiting longer is safe in the one direction that matters: B takes 9 burn
# damage a hit and may be dead by the end, but "assert pawn" resolves through
# corpses and the Burn hediff stays on the pawn inside one.
#
# B must stay up: ValidReplacementTarget rejects a downed candidate, so
# downing B would make the retarget impossible. What B must not do is shoot
# back. With an armed Pirate B, the run of 2026-09-24 23:51 ended with B
# carrying no hediff at all - twenty retargeted shots at 0.5 cannot all miss,
# so Bernael had stopped firing or B had left the line of sight. B is
# therefore a Colonist kind in the enemy faction: BasePlayerPawnKind has no
# weaponTags and no weaponMoney, so B spawns unarmed and without headgear,
# still up, still hostile, still a valid replacement. Bernael is drafted so a
# hostile in reach does not make them flee or drop the attack.
#
# The line after the tick is there for the next red run: if Bernael went
# down, it fails first and says so, and only a Bernael still standing leaves
# the Burn line to blame the retarget itself. Bernael's job is not asserted:
# once B is dead the remaining shots go to A, and when A dies the attack ends
# as it should.

requires dlc=Biotech
spawn Pawn:Colonist at 0,0 name="Bernael" xenotype=BX_Bernael
spawn Pawn:Pirate at 8,0 name="Pirate A" faction=enemy
spawn Pawn:Colonist at 8,3 name="Pirate B" faction=enemy
spawn Thing:BX_SoulLantern at 1,0
equip "Bernael" thing=BX_SoulLantern

down "Pirate A"
draft "Bernael"
attack "Bernael" target="Pirate A"

tick 1320 reason="four cycles of warmup 120, burst 5x20 and cooldown 120, plus flight"
assert pawn "Bernael" downed expect=absent
assert pawn "Pirate B" hediff=Burn expect=present

undraft "Bernael"
